WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.769
-After officially announcing
his re-election bid,

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:06.539
the president spent the week
rambling in phone interviews

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.674
while his administration
threatened war with Iran.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.943
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.412
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.448 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.883
After his campaign kickoff rally
on Tuesday,

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:20.719
Trump decided to relive
the evening last night

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:22.889
by calling up one of his
most loyal servants,

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.858
Fox News host Sean Hannity,

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:28.761
and he turned almost the
entirety of his hour-long show

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.496
over to the president
and grilled him

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.633
with hard hitting questions
about the 2020 campaign.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.736
-Joining us now is the president
of the United States.

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:39.271
President Trump, sir, good to
have you back on the program.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:40.906
-Hi, Sean.

00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:46.446
-You seem to really love doing
what you did last night.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.781
It looked like tailgating party.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:51.283
I actually kind of regretted
not going

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.385
because I wanted to hang out
with the people outside

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:54.954
because they were
having a blast.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.890
There's 20-some-odd candidates.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.192
I want to get your general
thoughts on all of them.

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:03.429
-I look at some of them.

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.698
I don't see George Washington.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.233
I don't see Churchill.

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:12.738
I don't see anybody in
particular that I worry about.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:15.074
-I don't see George Washington,
either, sir.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.143
-Ugh. What a suck up.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.944
"I don't see George Washington
either, sir.

00:01:18.944 --> 00:01:19.979
You're so funny, sir.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.548
I wish I could tailgate with
you, sir.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.116
Do you like my new haircut, sir?

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:26.752
I started wearing my tie down to
my crotch just like you, sir.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.855
Just like you, sir."

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.156
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:34.561
Also, what do you mean
you don't see Winston Churchill.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.429
You're no Winston Churchill,
either, buddy.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.598
I don't care if you
tried on a Churchill-style hat

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.100
when you were in the UK.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.404
You don't look like Churchill.
You look like Hardy ate Laurel.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.172
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.542
And Trump, of course, loves
to bask in this mindless praise,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.378
which is why he once again
droned on for so long

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.447
that even Hannity couldn't get
him off the phone.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.716
This has happened with Fox News
hosts before, but this time,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.217
Hannity had to hand it over

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.752
to the next fawning
Trump sycophant,

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.554
Laura Ingraham, whose show
started after Hannity's.

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:05.958
Again, this was like 45 minutes
into the interview.

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.460
-Our military
is almost completed

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.863
in terms of being rebuilt.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:15.034
And we are doing missile
and missile technology

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.036
that nobody's even seen before.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.738
-Mr. President --
-I'm thinking about,

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.706
"Do we announce it
or do we not announce it?"

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:22.908
Because I've said,
you got to pay for NATO.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:24.877
You know, the United States was
paying for NATO.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.512
-Mr. President --
-You had a lot of countries

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.514
that were delinquent.
I think we're gonna --

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:29.949
-Mr. President...
-I hope we're going to have

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.785
a good relationship, but we're
a very strong country again,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.721
and we're respected again, Sean.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:38.291
&gt;&gt; I hate to interrupt you,
but I actually took 15 minutes

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.993
of Laura Ingraham's show.
-This keeps happening.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.729
He's a meandering old man
rambling on the phone

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.197
about nonsense
and even his friends

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:46.366
can't get him to hang up.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.035
Like, where is he even
making these calls?

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.337
Is he wandering around
the White House lawn

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.306
in his bathrobe?

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.608
At some point, you expect to
hear a nurse on the other end

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:56.909
screaming,
"There you are, Donald!

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.010
Come back to the White House!

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.880
You have to eat
your pureed carrots!"

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.782
[ As Trump ] But I don't --
I don't want my carrots.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.950
That's where they hide
the medicine.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.053
And I mean...

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.588
[ Normal voice ]
And then, after that,

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:11.724
it got even worse because
Hannity actually had to

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.025
hand Trump over to Ingraham,

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:15.528
and Trump still wouldn't
stop talking.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.863
-I actually took 15 minutes
of Laura Ingraham's show.

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:20.166
But I want to tell you --
-I know that. I noticed that.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:22.234
Laura must not be happy
right now.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.603
-It's her birthday today, sir.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.805
-She's a great person.
'Cause I'll tell you what --

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:29.442
I've known her for a long time.
She's great person.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.776
-And thank you
for being with us.

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.211
Laura, happy birthday from me.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.679
And the president, I think,

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.514
would like to wish you
happy birthday.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.717
-That's right.
-Hey, Mr. President.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:40.787
Thank you. Happy birthday.
Wow, that's great.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.556
-We've known each other
a long time,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.724
and congratulations
on your show.

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:48.961
-They're just passing him around
like when your grandpa calls

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:54.267
on Easter and everyone has
to take turns saying hello.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.669
Uh-huh. Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:59.471
Oh! Oh! Here's Karen!
I'm gonna hand you to Karen.

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:03.076
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.960
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look...

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.463
Lookit, even Hannity --
Hannity throwing up his hands.

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.465
Even he can't believe it.

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:28.801
At this point, he could just
stop showing up to work

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:32.705
and change the name of his show
to "Grandpa's on the Phone."

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.874
So Trump rambled on the phone
for almost an hour

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.942
about meaningless nonsense,
and yet,

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.311
when you actually want him
to go into detail

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.245
about something important
like, say, his administration's

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:42.782
march to war with Iran,
he's much more tight-lipped.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.250
Today in the Oval Office, he was
asked about reports that Iran

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.785
shot down an unmanned US drone.

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:48.954
Now, Iran says the drone
was in its airspace.

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.189
Trump on the other hand,
said the drone

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.457
was over international waters,

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.059
but his explanation
didn't provide many details.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:56.962
-Iran made a big mistake.

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:59.765
This drone was in international
waters, clearly.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.300
We have it all documented.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.203
It's documented scientifically,
not just words.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.005
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.307
Well...

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.775
if it's documented
scientifically,

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:11.411
I feel so much better.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:14.247
If there's anyone I trust with
science, it's Donald Trump.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:17.149
I could definitely see him
in a lab coat and goggles

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:19.419
writing down a proof
on a chalkboard.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.452
"What did you find, Donald?"

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:22.522
[ As Trump ] I -- I fou--
I ate the chalk.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:24.189
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:27.459
I ate the chalk
before I was done.

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:28.961
[ Normal voice ] It's important
to note that Trump

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.130
can't just unilaterally
go to war with Iran.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.466
The Constitution says he needs
authorization from Congress,

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.901
which he does not have.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.036
And even though he spent
two years flouting the law,

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.470
during his rally on Tuesday,

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.839
Trump lied and claimed he would
protect the Constitution

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:43.008
and even said Democrats
were the ones destroying it.

00:05:43.008 --> 00:05:48.447
-Imagine if we had a Democrat
president and Democrat congress

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:50.483
in 2020.

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:54.620
They would strip Americans
of their Constitutional rights.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.958
This election is a verdict
on whether we want to live

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:02.628
in a country where the people
who lose an election

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:07.299
refuse to concede
and spend the next two years

00:06:07.299 --> 00:06:10.403
trying to shred our
Constitution.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.404
-Dude, you tried to stop
an investigation

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:13.739
of your own campaign

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:15.507
and you called a fake
national emergency

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:17.209
to build a border wall
on your own.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:19.912
The only way you could care less
about the Constitution

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.849
is if it was written in Spanish.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.416
I doubt Trump could identify

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:26.352
even one of the founding
fathers.

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:28.353
If you showed him a picture of
John Adams and said,

00:06:28.353 --> 00:06:29.422
"Who's this?" He'd go,

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.858
[ As Trump ]
Uh, is it Paul Giamatti?

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.891
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.891 --> 00:06:34.227
[ Normal voice ]
In fact, as we speak,

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:36.028
Trump is waging war on congress,

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.997
instructing aides to defy
subpoenas

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.899
and refusing to turn over
his tax returns

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:42.334
or financial records, even
though Trump keeps claiming,

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:45.371
as he did in his ABC interview
on Sunday that he wants

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:48.841
some unspecified financial
statement to be made public,

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.743
or rather, he tried
to make that claim,

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:53.045
but was interrupted by
a staffer in the room.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.246
-At some point,
I hope they get it 'cause...

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:56.315
-[ Coughing ]
...it's a fantastic

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.917
financial statement.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:00.886
It's a fantastic
financial statement.

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:02.388
And -- Let's do that over.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.023
He's coughing in the middle
of my answer.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:05.924
-Yeah. Okay.
-I don't like that, you know?

00:07:05.924 --> 00:07:07.393
I don't like that.
-Your Chief of Staff.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.128
-If you are going to cough,
please leave the room.

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:11.797
-Get a shot
and I'll come over here.

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.100
-Sorry.
-You just can't cough.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.902
-Just to change the shadow.
Sorry, Mr. Trump.

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:18.904
-Okay. Do you want to do that
a little differently then?

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:20.873
-Yeah, we just change the angle.
Yep.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:23.876
-Thank you.
-So at some point...

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:27.146
-Look, I -- I know we've all
talked about the coughing,

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:29.682
but look at him glaring
at the camera like that.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:31.717
This looks like one of those
nature videos

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:35.187
where a lion finds a night
vision camera in a bush.

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:37.790
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.992
So Trump's just brazenly
defying subpoenas

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.860
in violation of
the Constitution and the law.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.862
In fact, Trump's White House
even instructed

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:45.832
his former Communications
Director, Hope Hicks,

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:49.268
to defy a subpoena for documents
and refuse to answer questions

00:07:49.268 --> 00:07:50.636
whence she testified yesterday

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.171
in front of the House
Judiciary Committee.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:54.840
The White House argued that
Hicks is absolutely immune

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.176
from being compelled to answer
questions about her time

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.944
as a senior advisor
to the president.

00:07:58.944 --> 00:08:01.280
Well, there we go.
She has absolute immunity.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.314
There's just one problem --

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:04.116
No one knows
what the hell that means.

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:07.953
-There is no such thing
as absolute immunity.

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:10.289
It just doesn't exist.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:11.757
So I can't even explain to you

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.325
what they could
or couldn't assert.

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:15.928
Because as far as I can tell,
it's a made-up term.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:19.865
-Absolute immunity sounds like
a hair growth supplement

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:22.034
they sell at GNC.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:24.570
This is totally the Trump
administration's style --

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.905
When the existing legal terms
aren't working out for them,

00:08:26.905 --> 00:08:28.340
they just invent some new ones.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.709
They're like kids on a
playground daring each other

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:31.844
to lick a frozen pole.

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:33.279
"I have absolute immunity."

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.281
"Oh, yeah? Well, I have
double dog absolute immunity."

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:38.184
"Well, I have triple dog secret
immunity, no take backs."

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.285
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:41.153
Trump's promise to restore
the Constitution

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:42.387
was just another lie,

00:08:42.387 --> 00:08:44.623
and another in a long list
of broken promises.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:46.224
And now that he's running
for re-election,

00:08:46.224 --> 00:08:48.260
Trump and his team
are criticizing Democrats

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.996
for supposedly making promises
they can't keep,

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:54.500
as his son Don Jr. did at that
re-election rally on Tuesday.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:58.637
-Joe Biden comes out, "Well,
if you elect me president,

00:08:58.637 --> 00:09:00.940
I'm gonna cure cancer."

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:04.143
Well, why the hell didn't you
do that

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:06.479
over the last 50 years, Joe?

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:07.713
-You know what
we need to cure --

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:09.482
whatever the hell is growing on
your face.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:13.119
Because it's definitely
not a beard.

00:09:13.119 --> 00:09:16.822
You look like a little kid going
as a hobo for Halloween.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:20.358
I think you might be using
your Absolute Immunity wrong.

00:09:20.358 --> 00:09:24.296
Also, what do you mean,
we should have cured cancer

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:26.165
50 years ago?

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:28.133
That's not how scientific
progress works.

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:29.201
It takes time.

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:30.536
When the iPhone first came out,

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:33.305
nobody said, "Um, why the hell
didn't we have these

00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:36.274
during World War II?"

00:09:36.274 --> 00:09:40.045
There's even an app that helps
you find Nazis.

00:09:40.045 --> 00:09:41.513
But, hey, there you go.

00:09:41.513 --> 00:09:44.950
Politicians who make outlandish
promises like curing cancer

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.486
should not be believed, got it.

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:52.624
-We will come up with the cures
to many, many problems,

00:09:52.624 --> 00:09:58.431
to many many diseases,
including cancer and others.

00:09:58.431 --> 00:10:02.868
We will lay the foundation
for landing American astronauts

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:04.870
on the surface of Mars.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.806
-Amazing. Not only did he say
the exact same thing

00:10:07.806 --> 00:10:10.075
a few hours later, he went even
further and said

00:10:10.075 --> 00:10:11.844
we would land on Mars.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:14.679
And to promise a cure for cancer
as well as a trip to Mars

00:10:14.679 --> 00:10:15.914
is pretty cocky for a guy

00:10:15.914 --> 00:10:19.051
who's only about 35 bricks
into his wall.

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:20.118
[ Laughter ]

00:10:20.118 --> 00:10:22.021
[ As Trump ] This wall...

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:28.093
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:28.093 --> 00:10:29.928
This wall is a lot harder
than I thought.

00:10:29.928 --> 00:10:31.964
Should we --
Should we just do cancer?

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:35.634
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:39.704
Should we bail on the wall
and do cancer?

00:10:39.704 --> 00:10:42.641
This week, we've seen the core
of Trump on full display.

00:10:42.641 --> 00:10:45.311
He views the law not as
a constraint on his power,

00:10:45.311 --> 00:10:47.079
but as a weapon to be used
against others,

00:10:47.079 --> 00:10:49.448
and he's making wild promises
because he's failed

00:10:49.448 --> 00:10:51.216
on the ones he already made.

00:10:51.216 --> 00:10:53.219
Not only should he be impeached,
we should send him somewhere

00:10:53.219 --> 00:10:54.886
